1
00:00:00,368 --> 00:00:03,768
Before we launch either agent, look at
the workspace badge.

2
00:00:03,843 --> 00:00:08,064
It says Corporate G C P, and the
terminal is open in that workspace.

3
00:00:08,677 --> 00:00:11,377
That's the operating boundary for this
series.

4
00:00:11,427 --> 00:00:14,802
The repository in the demo is a
synthetic order service.

5
00:00:14,852 --> 00:00:19,327
We'll start with a read-only task, so by
the end you can compare exactly what the

6
00:00:19,377 --> 00:00:21,703
agent explored with what changed on
disk.

7
00:00:23,210 --> 00:00:27,960
In the terminal, run P W D, then Git
status and Git rev-parse.

8
00:00:28,010 --> 00:00:30,185
The path ends in training-orders.

9
00:00:30,285 --> 00:00:33,910
Status displays the lab branch and no
file entries beneath it,

10
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:35,677
so we have a clean starting point.

11
00:00:36,311 --> 00:00:39,361
The short commit is twenty-seven E four
A B one.

12
00:00:39,436 --> 00:00:41,636
Copy the commit from your own terminal.

13
00:00:41,686 --> 00:00:44,367
You can use it later to reproduce the
same inspection.

14
00:00:45,897 --> 00:00:48,372
Now ask each client for its version.

15
00:00:48,447 --> 00:00:52,147
This is much faster than guessing from
the menu or from a video.

16
00:00:52,222 --> 00:00:54,802
Record the two values your workspace
reports.

17
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:59,080
If one command is missing, you can
finish the first inspection with the

18
00:00:59,130 --> 00:01:00,980
other approved client.

19
00:01:01,055 --> 00:01:05,280
Use those version numbers when you look
up configuration, model selection,

20
00:01:05,330 --> 00:01:06,809
or skill discovery later.

21
00:01:08,313 --> 00:01:12,163
Open the existing session's model
selector or status view.

22
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:15,213
Suppose the client shows a friendly
model label.

23
00:01:15,288 --> 00:01:19,038
Record the resolved identifier when the
workspace makes it visible,

24
00:01:19,113 --> 00:01:21,592
since the same label can point to
different versions.

25
00:01:22,226 --> 00:01:24,426
Then check the configured provider.

26
00:01:24,476 --> 00:01:28,926
The terminal runs in G C P, while the
configured provider determines where

27
00:01:28,976 --> 00:01:30,622
model requests are processed.

28
00:01:31,253 --> 00:01:33,616
Keep both facts in the session record.

29
00:01:35,081 --> 00:01:37,956
Here is the effective policy for our
example:

30
00:01:38,031 --> 00:01:42,231
reading the training files is allowed,
and edits or unit-test runs ask for

31
00:01:42,281 --> 00:01:43,051
confirmation.

32
00:01:43,679 --> 00:01:46,554
Look up the effective policy for your
own session.

33
00:01:46,629 --> 00:01:49,154
This matters even for a simple prompt.

34
00:01:49,229 --> 00:01:51,554
You can tell an agent to inspect a file,

35
00:01:51,604 --> 00:01:55,054
but a proposed command is still a
separate action that needs to fit the

36
00:01:55,104 --> 00:01:56,168
session's permissions.

37
00:01:57,668 --> 00:02:02,118
Ask the agent for two paths and one
concrete case: the quantity validator,

38
00:02:02,318 --> 00:02:04,718
its test file, and the test for zero.

39
00:02:04,793 --> 00:02:06,339
Watch it inspect the checkout.

40
00:02:06,941 --> 00:02:11,591
The example points to the validator in
orders slash quantity dot P Y and to

41
00:02:11,641 --> 00:02:13,759
test rejects zero in the test suite.

42
00:02:14,348 --> 00:02:17,842
Those names give us a simple way to
confirm the answer ourselves.

43
00:02:19,310 --> 00:02:22,160
Open the reported validator and the
test.

44
00:02:22,235 --> 00:02:26,435
Check that the test actually passes zero
to the validator and expects a

45
00:02:26,485 --> 00:02:27,130
rejection.

46
00:02:27,754 --> 00:02:30,329
Then run the branch and commit checks
again.

47
00:02:30,404 --> 00:02:34,179
In the demonstration the branch header
is still the only status line,

48
00:02:34,229 --> 00:02:35,810
and the commit is unchanged.

49
00:02:36,444 --> 00:02:39,319
That gives us direct evidence about the
checkout,

50
00:02:39,369 --> 00:02:41,214
independent of the agent's summary.

51
00:02:42,706 --> 00:02:47,196
Finish by saving the workspace, commit,
client version, model, provider,

52
00:02:47,361 --> 00:02:50,561
and permissions next to the two verified
paths.

53
00:02:50,636 --> 00:02:53,125
That's the minimum useful record for the
next lab.

54
00:02:53,739 --> 00:02:57,664
You can now start a session with a clear
boundary, ask a small question,

55
00:02:57,784 --> 00:02:59,759
and verify the answer.

56
00:02:59,859 --> 00:03:03,742
Next, we'll check how both clients pick
up the same repository convention.
